		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4976&amp;p=36293#p36293"><![CDATA[
btw, this are the original calibration values from the radio, and the power values seems to be ok<br><br><img src="https://i.imgur.com/e6ilYeD.png" class="postimage" alt="Image"><br><img src="https://i.imgur.com/5Pf65SQ.png" class="postimage" alt="Image"><br><br>and...<br><br>the values for 1W in opengd77 match the same values as in the original calibration data for low power <img alt="👍" class="emoji smilies" draggable="false" src="//twemoji.maxcdn.com/2/svg/1f44d.svg"><br><br>but...<br><br>the values for 2W in opengd77 are high and does not match the values in the original calibration for mid power<br><br>the values for 5W in opengd77 are higher and does not match with the values in the original calibration for high power<br><br>also <strong class="text-strong">the values in 5W in opengd77 for 460mhz, 470mhz and 480mhz are completely low</strong>.<br><br><img src="https://i.imgur.com/fuoiIdf.png" class="postimage" alt="Image"> <img src="https://i.imgur.com/22kJyxz.png" class="postimage" alt="Image"> <img src="https://i.imgur.com/nDXz1r0.png" class="postimage" alt="Image"><br><br>so, seems OpenGD77 is not getting/calculating/applying the proper values for 5W in 460Mhz, 470Mhz and 480Mhz.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=4191">MELERIX</a> — Wed Mar 19, 2025 3:59 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
