		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4976&amp;p=36281#p36281"><![CDATA[
hello, currently I have in my hands a DM-1701 from a friend, and I have installed OpenGD77 on it (the current BETA 2025 03 16)<br><br>but I've noticed a strange behavior with power settings, for example in a UHF test repeater in 470 mhz, if I put the radio in 5W the radio TX never reach the repeater, but if I put the radio in 4W, 3W or 2W it reach the repeater without troubles.<br><br>currently I don't have a power meter but I've tested in my SDR in a random simplex frequency, let's say for example 471 in simplex, and if I put the radio in 5W the power in the spectrum looks is a bit low, but if I put 4W, 3W o 2W the power in the spectrum looks normal.<br><br>so I'm wondering maybe is a OpenGD77 issue? because with the factory stock firmware, the power is ok when is in High mode.<br><br>NOTE 1: in VHF it works normally, the issue is only in UHF mode.<br>NOTE 2: testing with a blank opengd77 codeplug or even resetting the settings does not make any difference.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=4191">MELERIX</a> — Wed Mar 19, 2025 1:13 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
